    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0227" n="95" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg95"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 56 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to Prime Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d56-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-11">11 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Your 82.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d56-f2"/> I am in agreement and will instruct
                        Eisenhower to make the necessary
                    arrangements to accomplish your expressed desires.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d56-f3"
                    />
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d56-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d56-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d56-f2" n="2" xml:id="d56-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="#d55">document No. 55</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d56-f3" n="3" xml:id="d56-f3-content">
                <p>On June 12, in telegram No. W–15519, General of the
                    Army George C. Marshall sent to
                        Eisenhower the text of the final
                    paragraph of <ref target="#d55">document No. 55</ref>, prefaced with the
                    following instruction (Department of the Army Files): <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The <hi rendition="#small-caps">President</hi> directs that you make
                            necessary advance arrangements to accomplish the desires expressed in
                            the following quoted message from 
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Churchill</hi>
                             with which he is in agreement.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
